# Day 1 – Learning Notes

## Objectives Achieved

* Understood the business requirements of a Placement Management System.
* Designed a Salesforce data model based on real-world requirements.
* Created custom objects and established relationships between them.
* Practiced writing SOQL queries to retrieve and filter data.
* Developed an Apex class to implement business logic.
* Implemented an Apex Trigger to validate student eligibility before creating an application.

## Key Concepts Learned

* Salesforce Custom Objects
* Custom Fields
* Lookup Relationships
* SOQL Basics
* Relationship Queries
* Apex Classes
* Apex Triggers
* Business Logic Implementation

## Skills Gained

* Designing Salesforce data models.
* Writing efficient SOQL queries.
* Creating reusable Apex methods.
* Implementing validation using Before Insert Triggers.
* Understanding how Salesforce automates business processes.

## Outcome

Successfully built the foundation of the Placement Management System by implementing the data model, SOQL queries, Apex class, and trigger-based validation.
